  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "CRSBench-HintGenerator",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/your-org/crsbench",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-122",
              "name": "CWE-122: Heap-based Buffer Overflow",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Heap-based Buffer Overflow"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-787",
              "name": "CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Out-of-bounds Write"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Out-of-bounds Write"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CWE-193",
              "name": "CWE-193: Off-by-one Error",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Off-by-one Error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Specific vulnerability type: Off-by-one Error"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-122",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-122 - Heap-based Buffer Overflow\nVulnerability: Off-by-One Heap Buffer Overflow in buffer_write\nDescription: A heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the buffer_write function\nin utils.c due to an incorrect bounds check. The function uses \"index > buf->size\"\ninstead of \"index >= buf->size\", allowing writes at an index equal to the buffer\nsize. This off-by-one error permits writing one byte past the end of the allocated\nheap buffer. When triggered via func_unicode_\u7834\u58ca with a crafted input containing\nspecific values (\u5909\u6570a=0x1337, \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u043c\u0435\u043d\u043d\u0430\u044f_b=0x1338, \u03bc\u03b5\u03c4\u03b1\u03b2\u03bb\u03b7\u03c4\u03ae_c=0x12c), the\nvulnerability allows an attacker to write at index 300 in a 300-byte buffer,\ncorrupting adjacent heap memory. This can lead to heap metadata corruption,\npotential arbitrary code execution, or denial of service.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "utils.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 24,
                  "endLine": 24,
                  "startColumn": 21,
                  "endColumn": 21
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "buffer_write",
                  "kind": "function"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-787",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-787 - Out-of-bounds Write\nVulnerability: Off-by-One Heap Buffer Overflow in buffer_write\nDescription: A heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the buffer_write function\nin utils.c due to an incorrect bounds check. The function uses \"index > buf->size\"\ninstead of \"index >= buf->size\", allowing writes at an index equal to the buffer\nsize. This off-by-one error permits writing one byte past the end of the allocated\nheap buffer. When triggered via func_unicode_\u7834\u58ca with a crafted input containing\nspecific values (\u5909\u6570a=0x1337, \u043f\u0435\u0440\u0435\u043c\u0435\u043d\u043d\u0430\u044f_b=0x1338, \u03bc\u03b5\u03c4\u03b1\u03b2\u03bb\u03b7\u03c4\u03ae_c=0x12c), the\nvulnerability allows an attacker to write at index 300 in a 300-byte buffer,\ncorrupting adjacent heap memory. This can lead to heap metadata corruption,\npotential arbitrary code execution, or denial of service.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
